  "source": {
    "plan": "Callboard row 2026-11-29 (storyhowto, story-howto), the earliest planned row on 2026-11-24; look collage per DIRECTION 2026-11-20 (the row said paper)",
    "project": "ppvqmbzuqvzpiuqaiqfy",
    "sql": "select m.id, m.character_name, m.estimated_duration_seconds, m.overdone_score, p.title, p.author, p.copyright_status from monologues m join plays p on p.id=m.play_id where m.id in (39672, 4518, 4385, 625)",
    "checked": "2026-11-24: monologue 39672 Lady Hunstanton (A Woman of No Importance, Oscar Wilde, play 50, 1893, public domain) 1:09, overdone 0; 625 Cassius (Julius Caesar, Shakespeare, 'I know that virtue to be in you, Brutus') 180s = 3:00, public domain. In the Ghost Light app 'comedic, under 90 seconds, Oscar Wilde' returns Lady Hunstanton 1:09, Lord Illingworth 1:18, Lord Augustus 1:04 first, 30 monologues",
    "changed_from_plan": "the row's search ('comedic, under 90 seconds') returns Jackie (The Comedian, a film, with its text) first and Philo (a row cut from an essay on Plautus, not a play) second, so the film types 'comedic, under 90 seconds, Oscar Wilde', which brings three public domain pieces under 90 seconds up first. Milo's long speech is named (Cassius, Julius Caesar) because its library length is exactly three minutes. The notice title card was dropped in the notice beat (the notice is the text). Total 26.6s",
    "app": "Ghost Light web preview built from actorrise main apps/mobile (7a66bbb) plus web-preview.patch, dark theme, demo account, 2026-11-24",
    "flow": "flows/search-ninety-seconds.json (shots -> public/story/2026-11-29-ninety-seconds/*.png)",
